{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774740,"nonce":"bWoquR0JWg6SH9Pxy9hDUJAyKFc=","title":"docs(adr): ADR-0060 is Accepted — all six slices are on main","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #83 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `docs/adr-0060-accepted` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-25T19:13:22Z · Merged: 2026-07-25T20:01:25Z\n\nTwo-line status change. ADR-0060 read `Proposed` while the work was in flight; all six slices have now landed (PRs #74, #75, #77, #82), so the record should say so.\n\nThis repo has form here — ADRs 0045–0054 sat marked `Proposed` for months after they were built, and a shipped decision reading as a proposal is how the next person mistrusts the whole index.\n\n**Not** rewriting the decision text. The one deviation is already recorded in part D: an unregistered `credential.secret_ref` is a DEGRADED warning rather than a boot refusal, because only the running server can PUT that secret and refusing would deadlock a fresh database.\n\n**What \"Accepted\" does not claim:** the Forgejo adapter has never been run against a real Forgejo. Its API shapes are asserted against unit tests of what we believe they are, and one wrong guess already shipped and was caught in #82 (`register_webhook` sent no `config.secret`, so every delivery would have been 401'd by our own endpoint). Tracked as git-bug `3863d5e`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}